# MAF Group Chat Backend

Backend-only group chat workflow built with Microsoft Agent Framework, Python, uv, and SSE streaming.

## Features

- FastAPI HTTP API
- Microsoft Agent Framework group chat orchestration
- SSE streaming for intermediate agent turns and final output
- In-memory thread, message, and run state for local development
- Provider abstraction for Foundry, Azure OpenAI, or OpenAI

## Quick Start

```bash
uv sync
cp .env.example .env
uv run uvicorn maf_backend.main:app --reload
```

## Environment

- `MODEL_PROVIDER`: `foundry`, `azure_openai`, or `openai`
- `FOUNDRY_PROJECT_ENDPOINT`, `FOUNDRY_MODEL`
- `AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT`, `AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY`, `AZURE_OPENAI_MODEL`
- `OPENAI_API_KEY`, `OPENAI_MODEL`

## API

- `POST /api/v1/threads`
- `GET /api/v1/threads/{thread_id}`
- `GET /api/v1/threads/{thread_id}/messages`
- `POST /api/v1/threads/{thread_id}/runs`
- `GET /api/v1/runs/{run_id}`
- `GET /api/v1/runs/{run_id}/events`

## Notes

This first version keeps state in memory and runs one process-local workflow per run. It is intended as a backend foundation that can later be extended with persistent storage and human-in-the-loop resume flows.
